Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: subscribe to encoded picture types

Korri-local patch against Linux v7.2. The decoder already subscribes to
HFI_PROP_PICTURE_TYPE and the response handler already maps it to V4L2
keyframe flags. Encoder sessions skip all subscriptions, leaving every
encoded packet unmarked, including real IDRs observed on the Odin 2 Portal.
Request the same property on the encoder bitstream port.

This is not an upstream commit. Remove when upstream reports encoder
picture types through the same V4L2 buffer flags.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -1060,8 +1060,17 @@
 
 	payload[0] = HFI_MODE_PROPERTY;
 
-	if (inst->domain == ENCODER)
-		return 0;
+	if (inst->domain == ENCODER) {
+		/* Raw input has no coded picture type. Request it on bitstream output. */
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane))
+			return 0;
+		payload[1] = HFI_PROP_PICTURE_TYPE;
+		return iris_hfi_gen2_session_subscribe_mode(inst,
+						HFI_CMD_SUBSCRIBE_MODE,
+						plane,
+						HFI_PAYLOAD_U32_ARRAY,
+						payload, 2 * sizeof(u32));
+	}
 
 	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane)) {
 		subscribe_prop_size = core->iris_firmware_data->dec_input_prop_size;
